# nr-office-pdf-write-core: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own)

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/lib.rs
Anchor: the module list, after `pub mod text;` (alphabetical order puts it last; `xref` stays where it is):

    pub mod write;

Anchor: the crate doc comment, last paragraph ("The modules after them ... never share one."): append
"`write` is the writing half (a mutable document over the same object model, the Info dictionary, save with or
without object streams)."

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/Cargo.toml
[dependencies]  add (flate2 is the encoder of the Flate streams the writer makes: object streams, the cross-reference
stream, content streams; the version and features are the workspace's, already in Cargo.lock):

    flate2 = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-workspace-hack = { version = "0.1", path = "../mixdog-workspace-hack" }   # if the hakari rule of the workspace wants it for a crate that gains a normal dependency

[dev-dependencies]  remove `flate2 = { workspace = true }` (it is a normal dependency now, tests/syntax.rs and
tests/twin_write_core.rs use it from there) and add:

    serde_json = { workspace = true }       # tests/twin_write_core.rs reads golden.json
    mixdog-testkit = { workspace = true }   # file reads/writes and the node process of the ignored live test

Cargo.lock (lead regenerates it offline, --locked after that): the `mixdog-pdf` package gains `mixdog-testkit` and
`serde_json` (flate2 is already listed there as a dev dependency). No new crate enters the lock.

## 3. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Run `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index` once the wave is merged: it adds the row
of the new set `office-write-core` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-write-core.mjs, 1 file,
golden.json). The set's own MANIFEST.json is already written (native/core/fixtures/office-write-core/MANIFEST.json).

## 4. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no desktop fragment. The tools that call the writer (the office PDF
operations, pdf-draw, OCR overlay, marks, batch structure) are other tasks of the track; they use
`mixdog_pdf::write::{PdfDocument, LoadOptions, SaveOptions, DocumentProperties}` and build the `StreamFilters` of
`LoadOptions` from mixdog-pdf-codec's filters (the ext-host codec glue), which this task does not depend on.
